+# Closed-source grouped meal-memory host candidate
+
+## Status and boundary
+
+This is source-only, uncompiled and unexecuted host integration on top of qualified core `a5b12af62dab4f167c003e48e4ca37fdda74d0c1`. The qualified core stays frozen separately. No GDE1, decoder-gradient credit or six-row repair is combined. No acquired life or checkpoint was read, reset, migrated, or pruned. No study seed was chosen. All native commands remain held for a renewed resource allocation.
+
+The new `CpuGroupedMealM2HostV1` has a distinct prefix, lineage and policy. Old `CpuCanonicalHost`, `CpuGroupedM2HostV1`, M1 and old envelope entry points do not select it. The new wrapper's old source/body state container is private, stored as exact UTF-8 beneath the new outer identity. There is no public old-checkpoint conversion. Its only construction path delegates fresh-body/source admission, while restore requires the new outer identity, matching source/mode and typed meal proof validation. Old bytes are rejected at the new prefix and vice versa. Nested legacy state retains exact existing codecs and sampler IEEE-bit handling; the outer round-trip rejects omitted/unknown fields and any rewriting of acquired bytes.
+
+## Explicit seams
+
+- `prepare_canonical_frame_with_meal_v1` duplicates the existing preparation path but selects the named meal reader at both baseline and routed recall. The old preparation body is unchanged.
+- `object_familiarity_with_meal_v1` groups bounded matching records by latest source sequence and sums the maximum observation count within each group. This is immediate-sibling protection only. Independently merged histories lack full lineage and can still overlap; these are not exact independent exposure counts. The old familiarity method is unchanged.
+- The separate host loop calls `observe_sealed_patch_with_meal_v1` once per original sealed event. It retains the representative and at most one exact tracked Ingest/Consumed association. It does not add a physical event, body advance, experience sequence, predictor target, neural execution, synaptic/optimizer update, or second debit.
+- One `MealMemorySleepProofV1` is retained per original replay event. The old representative projection is retained in the private base controller for its unchanged authority validator. Both lists advance/evict/clear together. This intentionally duplicates bounded metadata; actual envelope size and wall-time overhead are unmeasured.
+- `run_bounded_sleep_transaction_with_meal_v1` authenticates every proof, even unavailable ones; resolves up to two retained IDs per original event; deduplicates promoted IDs globally; and updates each eligible predictor target and eligibility sample once. Bank and sidecar are unchanged by candidate sleep resolution. Predictor/topology changes stage and commit atomically.
+- `MealSleepWorkReceiptV1` is a new receipt/schema/domain. It permits unique promoted IDs up to twice the number of original events, requires predictor updates equal eligible events, and derives exact declared work units. The old one-ID-per-event receipt remains strict and byte-identical.
+
+## Pricing and physiology
+
+Waking `memory_ops` already counts recall bucket reads and similarity evaluations; it does not price ordinary association writes. This candidate explicitly keeps both ordinary and supplemental waking association writes unpriced under that inherited contract. It makes no claim that their execution is free. Added retained records may increase later actual retrieval work. Sleep charges its existing measured work formula, including each unique promoted association, while replay and predictor counts remain per original event.
+
+Administrative cloning, hashing, proof validation and checkpoint serialization do not acquire a made-up biological penalty. There is no post-seal charge that would circularly change the meal valence or double-debit the body. A future write-price policy would require an explicit pre-seal reservation and qualification. No coefficient or chemistry is changed to manufacture meal coverage.
+
+## Authored controls, not native results
+
+Fourteen new core cases cover two associations/one event, one surviving association, all-unavailable work, merged IDs, malformed unavailable siblings, duplicate/missing/reordered proofs, atomic late failures, portable cold continuation, owners/profiles/legacy rejection, actual bank capacity, old receipt bytes and immediate-sibling familiarity. They have not run on this source revision.
+
+Four host cases are authored:
+
+1. Existing fixed-source no-food scene compares old closed state bytes against the new private state container, rejects opposite envelope identities, and checks exact cold continuation with frozen optimizer/synapses.
+2. An actual sampler test runs eight intervals in the same fixed-source registered-body scene with nearby ordinary harmless food. It reports physical Consumed receipts, supplemental proofs and retained associations separately. If it misses the nonrepresentative branch, it must be reported as missing coverage, not changed into a forced success or called autonomous learning.
+3. A separately labeled registered-world scripted Rest+Eat intervention uses one real source execution and the real world action/biology boundary. Only a test-only callback replaces the selected joint action while preserving typed policy/frame bindings. It changes no logits, coefficients, source genome or chemistry and never claims to be the sampler's draw. Preparatory Touch/acquisition remains non-Consumed; the positive control requires an actual world Consumed receipt and a retained supplemental association, then exact cold continuation. The production path always uses the unmodified sampler call.
+4. A committing host positive control precedes missing/duplicate proof, wrong policy and late-sampling failure checks; failures must leave the original host unchanged.
+
+These controls reuse the pre-existing grouped-host unit fixture seed `0x0347_5250_484F_5354`. This is a test fixture, not a new study seed. No host case is described as passing until native compilation/execution is separately allocated and recorded.
+
+## Next review and native gates
+
+For Astra 6.2 or the next reviewer: check the wrapper's source authority/cold boundaries, duplicated proof storage and pruning synchronization, both recall calls, familiarity's limited historical claim, exact physical target binding, new sleep receipt capacity/work validation, and the test-only scripted versus actual-sampled distinction. Preserve the qualified-core patch and every failed source revision.
+
+After explicit renewed allocation, compile/list new core and host cases before running serially. Report compiler failures and zero-test filters exactly. Run the new core cases, prior 164-case core packet, actual registered scripted control, fixed sampled coverage report, opposite-envelope rejection, old closed literal-byte witness and exact next-packet cold continuation across admitted sleep. Measure target growth, envelope/raw resident size, clone/hash wall time and actual physical versus stored/recalled counts. Do not expand the study, combine decoder learning, or infer biological efficacy from these controls.
+
+Methodological reference: https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/ experiments 4/5/6. It motivates local, inspectable interventions and controls; it does not validate this artificial biology.
